      "text": "well, people on both sides wanted to stay together IN PRINCIPLE. But how exactly 'stay together' should work on the constitutional and economic level - fundamental and irreconcilable differences on both sides.    Good analogy would be marriage when both sides emotionally 'want to stay together', but can not even agree how to split the bills and if they live in an apartment or house, or even if 'external partners' are allowed or not:)    ...... yap, emotion is there, but marriage needs some fundamental agreement of how it should work ......     unsolvable. Great thing is all was solved amicably and there have never been hard feelings. Better to be good friends with some nostalgy regarding 'old times time together' than spending all the time in arguments without prospect of ever solving 'day-to-day rules'",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-25T21:59:15Z",
